  "body": "It would be great if WebIDL simply defined a single ES number type and allowed custom ranges. This would greatly simplify the spec by doing away with all the silly types: byte, short, etc. while remaining backwards compatible. \n\nSo, something like:\n\n```\ntypedef Number[−128..127] Byte;\n```\n\nAnd would allow for new types: \n\n```\ntypedef Number[0..360] Angle;\n```\n",
